offer.body=A growing town needs more than bigger piles of crates. Build me a warehouse and I will keep track of our stores and help you choose couriers. They will collect supplies where they are kept and carry them to the people who need them.
accepted.body=Here is the plan. Leave a clear path to the ledger desk so the couriers can collect supplies from general storage.
cancel=I need to put this project aside.
building.body=I will keep my things packed until the warehouse is ready. The plot plan lists the materials we need.
cancelled.body=All right. Find me when there is room for a proper storeroom.
back=Understood.
welcome.body=Now we can put things in order. Use the ledger desk to find your stores. Enable Logistics on the town journal's Work page when you need someone to carry supplies.
how.body=General storage holds the supplies you deposit. Crafted goods have their own collection space, while each production building keeps its own output and capacity. Couriers collect from the actual store, then carry supplies to a workplace. Their weekly wages appear with the town bills.
